# Generated by the Dart toolchain. Machine-specific and never part of the
# source: `package_config.json` records absolute local paths, and the compiled
# test snapshot plus `incremental_kernel.*` are tied to the exact SDK version
# that produced them. Committing any of this makes a fresh checkout either fail
# to resolve or silently run a stale kernel.
.dart_tool/

# Legacy, pre-2.15 package resolution. Unused here, but a stray file from an old
# checkout would still be picked up by tooling.
.packages

# Output of `dart run build_runner`.
build/

# `pubspec.lock` is deliberately NOT ignored. This package is `publish_to: none`
# and consumed from the app in the same repository rather than from pub.dev, so
# the lock is the record of the exact resolved dependency set the tests were
# verified against. For a package published to pub.dev the convention is the
# opposite, and this line is the one to revisit if that ever changes.
